399:\textit{Naive Schweitzer multi-server BS} (\texttt{W = L · (1 + Q · (N − 1) / (N · c))}) resulted in a 17--50\% error versus \texttt{SolverLN}, making it too inaccurate to be a candidate. \textit{Krzesinski Linearizer (\texttt{pfqn\_linearizermsKt})} (\texttt{PB = 2·sumQ/(pop+1-nservers)}) goes negative when \texttt{nservers $\approx$ ntot}, which the project's specific input shape of INF-folded inputs forced. \textit{Plain Bard-Schweitzer (\texttt{pfqn\_bsKt})} returned per-server \texttt{Q} not total, meaning the patch would need a wrapper, so we abandoned in favour of an in-place implementation.
