###### CONTRIBUTION numbers ######
72:Name-based coupling collapses because \texttt{SolverLN.buildLayers} does not preserve node names. It prefixes every server with \texttt{T:} or \texttt{P:} and groups all clients into a single node named \texttt{Clients}, the only name shared across layers --- and \texttt{Clients} is always an infinite-server (IS) station whose utilisation is approximately 1. On the \texttt{lqn\_basic} fixture the solver returns throughputs of \texttt{2.0E8} and service times collapsed to \texttt{1.0E-8} across the board: \texttt{nameIndexMap} matches only on \texttt{Clients}, \texttt{updateThinkTimeFromUtilization} zeroes the Delay think times because IS-station utilisation $\approx$ 1 drives \texttt{z = N · (1 - U) / X} to zero, and \texttt{updateServiceTimeFromResidence} then collapses every demand to \texttt{Exp.fitMean(0)} $\approx$ \texttt{1e-8}. The coupling channel has to be rebuilt around what \texttt{buildLayers} actually shares: the \texttt{T:} / \texttt{P:} server prefixes.
88:\emph{Worked example (one coupling sweep).} Take a single ensemble submodel --- a closed queue with server demand $D=0.5$ behind a \texttt{Clients} delay with think time $Z=1$, populated by $N=3$ jobs. Exact MVA gives the per-population recursion $R(n)=D\,(1+Q(n{-}1))$, $X(n)=n/(Z+R(n))$, $Q(n)=X(n)\,R(n)$:
95:1 & $0.500$ & $0.667$ & $0.333$ \\
96:2 & $0.667$ & $1.200$ & $0.800$ \\
97:3 & $0.900$ & $1.579$ & $1.421$ \\
102:\noindent Feeding the converged $X=1.579$, $Q=1.421$ into the two coupling formulas gives $Z_{\text{callee\_host}}=(N-Q)/X=(3-1.421)/1.579=1.00$ (the time the task spends \emph{away} from its host server, here exactly the think time) and $R_{\text{task}}=Q/X=0.90$ (its residence), the two quantities the next sweep writes into the adjacent layer --- the whole coupling mechanism in miniature.
146:The three blind spots are three distinct topologies (Figure~\ref{fig:cs-step2-fixtures}); seen together they motivate reading the LQN graph directly rather than through the ensemble's prefix indexing. (Grey = Immediate / zero-demand task; $Z$ = own think time.)
